implementationPlan.description:
A frozen mode that hides ONLY behind skip-worktree (DoD 1 and 2), byte-identical in scripts/tests/postflight.sh (the FROZENJS heredoc) and scripts/tests/postflight.ps1 ($frozenSuite).

Add the mode `skip-worktree-mutation` beside `hidden-mutation`. Its gate:
- runs `update-index --skip-worktree` on `owned.txt` and rewrites it;
- runs `update-index --skip-worktree` on the tracked `../seed.txt` (the repo-root file) and deletes it;
- exits 0.
There is no assume-unchanged anywhere in the mode. It covers both "edits or deletes".

Add it to every list that names `hidden-mutation`:
- the modes array;
- the `failed` list;
- the PUSH-BLOCKED list;
- the wantOutcome `inconclusive` list;
- the block asserting exactly one check run, exit 0 and outcome 'inconclusive'.
The mode then proves the run is classified inconclusive AND refused (PUSH-BLOCKED, the branch unmoved) on both wrappers.

Make the identical edit in both files, then confirm the two suites are byte-identical:
`cmp <(sed -n '/<<.FROZENJS.$/,/^FROZENJS$/p' scripts/tests/postflight.sh | sed '1d;$d') <(sed -n '/frozenSuite, @.$/,/^.@, \[Text/p' scripts/tests/postflight.ps1 | sed '1d;$d')`

Iterate with `MOE_FROZEN_TEST_ONLY=skip-worktree-mutation,hidden-mutation,wt-hidden,wt-assume,wt-pass,pass`. That runs only the frozen suite; postflight.ps1 exits after it. Run it through postflight.sh, and through postflight.ps1 under powershell.exe from a /mnt/d cwd (mem:gotcha-pwsh7-reachable-from-wsl: WSLENV=MOE_FROZEN_TEST_ONLY).

Mutants: record each one's result in the step note, on a scratch copy outside the checkout.
- (a) the old single combined pass in either wrapper: skip-worktree-mutation and wt-hidden must FAIL;
- (b) only the --no-assume-unchanged pass dropped: wt-assume must FAIL;
- (c) the exclude dropped from either pass: wt-pass must FAIL.
